<http://data.silknow.org/object/4e8656a8-b674-39fe-9a34-873ceb1ff5c2>
        a                              ecrm:E22_Man-Made_Object ;
        rdfs:comment                   "Tinsel print depicting Mr Osbaldiston in the character of Hardyknute in an unknown play. From an engraving published by M & B. Skelton, ca. 1840."@en , "The actor is depicted wearing a grey tunic, golden trousers and a dard red cloak. Holding a sword with his right hand."@en , "Tinsel print depicting Mr Osbaldiston in the character of Hardyknute in an unknown play. From an engraving published by M & B. Skelton, ca. 1840.\nTinsel prints were created from etched portraits of theatrical stars in popular roles they played on the London stage. They were hand-painted in watercolour and decorated with scraps of material and tinsel additions. They were popular during the first half of the 19th century and were considered an adult, rather than a child's hobby. By the 1830s it was possible to buy the tinsel, leather and feather ornaments to go with each image."@en ;
        ecrm:P138i_has_representation  <http://data.silknow.org/image/2ed6da35-b5a2-36ff-9fb3-6332d2682002> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note               "Tinsel print depicting Mr Osbaldiston in the character of Hardyknute in an unknown play. From an engraving published by M & B. Skelton, ca. 1840."@en , "The actor is depicted wearing a grey tunic, golden trousers and a dard red cloak. Holding a sword with his right hand."@en , "Tinsel print depicting Mr Osbaldiston in the character of Hardyknute in an unknown play. From an engraving published by M & B. Skelton, ca. 1840.\nTinsel prints were created from etched portraits of theatrical stars in popular roles they played on the London stage. They were hand-painted in watercolour and decorated with scraps of material and tinsel additions. They were popular during the first half of the 19th century and were considered an adult, rather than a child's hobby. By the 1830s it was possible to buy the tinsel, leather and feather ornaments to go with each image."@en ;
        ecrm:P43_has_dimension         <http://data.silknow.org/object/4e8656a8-b674-39fe-9a34-873ceb1ff5c2/dimension/2> , <http://data.silknow.org/object/4e8656a8-b674-39fe-9a34-873ceb1ff5c2/dimension/1> ;
        dc:identifier                  "S.36-1983" ;
